    "head_ref": "bot-policy-scope",
    "body": "[...] the policy would deny every bot.\r\n- Has-any-of groups without enclosing parens, which is how the server re-serializes them, are now recognized as simple expressions, so they open in the table editor. This also fixes Members policies.\r\n\r\nThis PR also fixes a bug where the test button fell back to `Test Access Rule`, which ignores the role. It now always uses `Simulate Access`, and shows a tooltip explaining why when it's disabled (simulation turned off on the server, or no permissions selected yet). Bug https://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-71299\r\n\r\n#### Screenshots\r\n\r\n<img width=\"983\" height=\"865\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-23 at 12 01 02 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/688261e5-18ff-4844-a215-eeb69d853759\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Ticket Link\r\nhttps://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-71033\r\nhttps://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-71299\r\n\r\n#### Release Note\r\n```release-note\r\nAdded a \"Bot accounts\" role to attribute-based permission policies in the System Console, so a policy can apply only to bot accounts. Bot accounts policies apply to requests made with a bot's access token or session, and take the place of Members policies for bots on the permissions they cover. As with other permission policies, once a Bot accounts policy covers a permission, users without a policy for that permission are denied it. Permission policies that target an unsupported role are now rejected.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Change Impact: 🔴 High\n\n**Changes Breakdown:**\n\n+674 -259 Production Changes (19.0%)  \n+3641 -327 Test Changes (81.0%)\n\n**Regression Risk:** The changes affect authorization policy roles, policy validation, and simulation across the server and web app. Tests cover many affected paths, but shared CEL utilities and policy flows can still cause regressions.\n\n*Generated by CodeRabbitAI*\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\r\n\n",
